<title>BELGIUM: Union Miniere sees $1,200 avge world zinc price.</title>
<headline>Union Miniere sees $1,200 avge world zinc price.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian non-ferrous metals company Union Miniere said on Thursday it expected an average world zinc price at around $1,200 per tonne in 1997.  </p>
<p>&quot;All the information we have shows that we can expect zinc prices of between $1,100 and $1,200 this year. A couple of weeks ago we thought it would be $1,150. Today I would bet on it being $1,200,&quot; UM chief executive officer Karel Vinck told a news conference on UM's 1996 results.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
